request.\r\n\r\nReusing previous TileMapLayer's `selection_pattern` causes the issue.\r\nThe change is to rudely call `selection_pattern.instantiate()` when the `tile_set_changed()` is called in class `TileMapLayerEditorTilesPlugin`. As `selection_pattern.instantiate()` is already there in the`_update_fix_selected_and_hovered()` function, simply get it out of the conditions.\r\n\r\nUpdate:\r\n\r\nFound that there's already a check for TileSet changes in `TileMapLayerEditorTilesPlugin::edit`. However, the `edited_layer` and `new_tile_map_layer` to be compared are pointing to the same location with given the `edited_tile_map_layer_id` both.\r\nChanged the id of `new_tile_map_layer` to `p_tile_map_layer_id`, which it should be in context.\r\n\r\nMany thanks to @groud 's help and advice.\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch in priority.\r\n\r\nRelevant fixes are cherry-picked for stable branches as needed by maintainers.\r\n\r\nTo speed up the contribution process and avoid CI errors, please set up pre-commit hooks locally:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/guidelines/code_style.html\r\n-->\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708059,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4MDU5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:2d","name":"topic:2d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.